          "id": "vulnerability:f1c2cc30-5181-5f4f-b57f-3f1db92b8b10",
          "type": "VULNERABILITY",
          "label": "CVE-2025-47277",
          "data": {
            "vulnerability_id": "54ef6f09-16cc-497e-8a1e-838ccf35d1f4",
            "cve_id": "CVE-2025-47277",
            "description": "### Impacted Environments\r\n\r\nThis issue ONLY impacts environments using the `PyNcclPipe` KV cache transfer integration with the V0 engine. No other configurations are affected.\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\nvLLM supports the use of the `PyNcclPipe` class to establish a peer-to-peer communication domain for data transmission between distributed nodes. The GPU-side KV-Cache transmission is implemented through the `PyNcclCommunicator` class, while CPU-side control message passing is handled via the `send_obj` and `recv_obj` methods on the CPU side.​ \r\n\r\nA remote code execution vulnerability exists in the `PyNc",
            "severity": "UNKNOWN",
            "cvss": [
